  ],
  "data_used": "riser: L 13.12 m between pinned joints, D 28 mm, EI 29.9 N m^2, mass ratio 3.0 with the internal water (paper; the page gives 1.85 kg/m), EA 5.88 MN, structural damping 0.33 % of critical, top spring 11.4 kN/m (page); the lower 5.94 m in the current (page); slide 3: towing speeds and mean top tensions of cases 1-9; slides 7-15: the measured envelopes along the riser (envelopes/); slides 17-19: the measured maximum cross-flow displacement, maximum mean and dynamic in-line displacement and overall standard deviations of curvature (measured_summary.csv); slide 23: the measured dominant cross-flow mode numbers",
  "extraction": "the slides are vector graphics: the measured points (filled circles of the measurement colour) and curves (polylines of 102 nearly equally spaced vertices along the riser, resampled to 101 equally spaced stations) are read as plotted coordinates and mapped linearly through the panel tick labels; the recovered towing speeds match slide 3 within 0.006 m/s; the envelope maxima of the mean in-line displacement match slide 17 within 0.05 D",
  "assumptions": "fresh water, Ca 1 (as L3-C); the 11.4 kN/m top spring of the two the page lists; the structural damping as bending damping of a pure bending mode at 2 Hz; the static top tension in the current (drag unamplified) set to the measured mean; the curvature panels of slides 7-15 have no scale, so each envelope curvature shape is scaled so that its r.m.s. over the stations equals the slide-19 overall standard deviation",
  "coefficients": "generic, not fitted to these measurements: Cl 0.8, cF 0.18, dF 0.08; in-line ClX 0.85, alpha 0.15 (Ulveseter et al. 2018); Cd 1.2; VIV AMPLITUDE Cv 0.8 constant with CdAmp = 1 + 2.3 s + 1.7 s^2, s = (A/D)/sqrt(2) (Chaplin et al. 2005a, Eq. 4); VIV DAMPING 0 0 1 (the amplification on the in-line drag only)",
